invariant: INV-17
file: quic_fail.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: quic_fail skips the Handshake receive key set, so a failed session
  keeps a key that opens the peer's packets, where INV-17 lets it keep only
  the write keys its one CONNECTION_CLOSE per level needs.
  test_close_after_failure requires every read key zero the moment the
  session fails.

--- old
    ct_wipe(&q->hs, sizeof q->hs);
    ct_wipe(&q->handshake_rx, sizeof q->handshake_rx);
--- new
    ct_wipe(&q->hs, sizeof q->hs);
